{"exportVersion":10,"dashboards":{"dashboard-1":{"title":"E-Commerce Clickstream: Real-Time Operations Dashboard","layout":[{"w":2,"h":1,"x":0,"y":0,"i":"item-1"},{"w":2,"h":1,"x":0,"y":1,"i":"item-2"},{"w":6,"h":2,"x":2,"y":0,"i":"item-3"},{"w":3,"h":2,"x":0,"y":2,"i":"item-4"},{"w":3,"h":2,"x":3,"y":2,"i":"item-5"},{"w":2,"h":2,"x":6,"y":2,"i":"item-6"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":0,"y":4,"i":"item-7"},{"w":3,"h":2,"x":4,"y":4,"i":"item-8"},{"w":1,"h":2,"x":7,"y":4,"i":"item-9"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":0,"y":6,"i":"item-10"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":4,"y":6,"i":"item-11"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":0,"y":8,"i":"item-12"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":4,"y":8,"i":"item-13"},{"w":5,"h":2,"x":0,"y":10,"i":"item-14"},{"w":1,"h":2,"x":5,"y":10,"i":"item-15"},{"w":2,"h":2,"x":6,"y":10,"i":"item-16"},{"w":4,"h":2,"x":0,"y":12,"i":"item-17"},{"w":8,"h":2,"x":0,"y":14,"i":"item-18"}],"description":"Sections ordered by derivation tier: (1) pipeline health / raw ingestion, (2) funnel & engagement from the clean user_events log, (3) cart lifecycle -> abandonment rate -> price/quantity concentration -> ranked product risk, (4) purchases -> AOV -> revenue by product, (5) system alerts and the final actionable worklist. No chart introduces a computed measure before its underlying raw field(s) have already been charted earlier in the same section.","embedding":{"anonymousAuthEnabled":true},"filters":[{"disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":true,"values":[]},"name":"Cart Status","linkedFields":[{"dataSourceId":"data-source-3","fieldPath":"status"}]},{"disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":true,"values":[]},"name":"Event Type","linkedFields":[{"dataSourceId":"data-source-1","fieldPath":"event_type"}]},{"disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":true,"values":[]},"name":"Alert Severity","linkedFields":[{"dataSourceId":"data-source-5","fieldPath":"severity"}]}]}},"items":{"item-1":{"title":"1.1 Behavioral Events Captured","description":"BASE (no derivation). Raw document count in user_events - the single-writer, non-duplicated behavioral log (Personalization Consumer only). Why it matters: this is the clean traffic-volume baseline every engagement chart in Section 2 is a slice of. Action: a stall here while purchases (4.1) keep flowing means a tracking outage, not fewer real visitors.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-1","iconValue":"number","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"value":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{},"channels":{"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Number","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"1bdc8bda-716e-42fc-9cc0-05adb61f9c58"}},"item-2":{"title":"1.2 Sessions Tracked","description":"BASE. Raw document count in session_funnel - one row per shopper session, written by the Session & Funnel Consumer. Why it matters: the denominator behind every funnel-stage and conversion insight in Section 2. Action: compare growth here against 1.1 - if events grow much faster than sessions, existing shoppers are browsing more, not new shoppers arriving.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-2","iconValue":"number","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"value":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{},"channels":{"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Number","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"9a203ce7-7f05-4def-97d4-ff228cd186af"}},"item-3":{"title":"1.3 Stream Throughput \u2014 Events per Minute by Topic","description":"BASE. Each cell = number of raw events any consumer logged in that minute, bucketed from event_timestamp. Deliberately NOT deduplicated across consumers (cart-events is subscribed to by all 3 roles, so it logs up to 3x) - this chart's job is only to prove the Kafka pipeline is alive and show relative topic load, not to count real traffic (use 1.1 for that). Action: a topic that goes flat here while others keep moving points to a stuck producer or consumer for that specific topic.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-7","iconValue":"heatmap","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[{"fieldPath":"minute_utc","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$dateToString\": {\n    \"format\": \"%m-%d %H:%M\",\n    \"date\": {\n      \"$dateFromString\": {\n        \"dateString\": \"$event_timestamp\",\n        \"onError\": null,\n        \"onNull\": null\n      }\n    },\n    \"timezone\": \"UTC\"\n  }\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$dateToString\":{\"format\":\"%m-%d %H:%M\",\"date\":{\"$dateFromString\":{\"dateString\":\"$event_timestamp\",\"onError\":null,\"onNull\":null}},\"timezone\":\"UTC\"}}"}],"channels":{"x":{"field":"minute_utc","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","transformedType":"String","channelType":"category"},"y":{"field":"_topic","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","transformedType":"String","channelType":"category"},"color":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{"categoryLabelAngle":{"enabled":true,"value":"diagonal"}}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Minute (UTC)"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Kafka topic"}},"color":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Events logged"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Heatmap","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"848c5934-db78-4ad3-b013-52229488dd02"}},"item-4":{"title":"2.1 Funnel Stage Distribution (Foundation Chart)","description":"BASE. Raw distribution of the stored field session_funnel.funnel_stage (view/search/click/cart/purchase) - each session counted once, at the furthest stage it ever reached. Why it matters: this is the foundation every conversion-rate claim in this dashboard rests on. Action: the biggest drop between two adjacent bars is the single highest-leverage stage to fix first.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-2","iconValue":"donut","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"label":{"field":"funnel_stage","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10","allOthers":true},"value":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"value":{}},"channels":{"label":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Funnel Stage"}},"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Donut","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"bc2534bd-6d65-4fd2-9eee-5515643977e7"}},"item-5":{"title":"2.2 Behavioral Event Volume by Type (Foundation Chart)","description":"BASE. Raw distribution of the stored field user_events.event_type - counted directly, no computation. Why it matters: foundation for 2.3, which drills into one slice of this same field. Action: a healthy funnel narrows gradually; a cliff between adjacent bars points to a specific stage problem, not general low traffic.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-1","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"y":{"field":"event_type","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Events"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Event Type"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"1602817b-6b37-4b58-9f9c-e1399306a4f8"}},"item-6":{"title":"2.3 Click Engagement by Placement (Drills Into 2.2)","description":"BASE. Raw distribution of the stored field click_target, filtered to event_type=click (one slice of 2.2). Why it matters: tells a manager which on-site placement - banner, nav, recommendation widget, search result - actually drives engagement. Action: reallocate creative/merchandising effort toward whichever placement leads this chart.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-1","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[{"fieldPath":"event_type","disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":false,"values":["click"]}}],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"y":{"field":"click_target","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Clicks"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Placement"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"7e2dffe4-2ace-4c9f-95b6-1aefea400e7e"}},"item-7":{"title":"2.4 Catalog Gaps \u2014 Zero-Result Search Terms","description":"BASE. Raw stored field 'count' in zero_result_search_terms - how many times each search term returned nothing, direct from the Personalization Consumer's own SEARCH_GAP_DETECTED tracking. Why it matters: every term here is a shopper who searched with real intent and found nothing to buy - a catalog or synonym-mapping gap, not a demand problem. Action: add the top terms to the catalog or map them to the nearest existing product category.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-6","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"count","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"sum"},"y":{"field":"term","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Zero-Result Occurrences"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Search Term"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"173830c3-d005-4abe-b699-29cf0929459a"}},"item-8":{"title":"3.1 Cart Outcome Breakdown (Foundation Chart)","description":"BASE. Raw distribution of the stored field cart_status.status - active/purchased/abandoned/emptied. Why it matters: the raw counts behind 3.2's derived rate - nothing later re-computes a rate without you first seeing these. Action: if 'abandoned' is the largest slice, prioritize the discount worklist (5.2) over top-of-funnel ad spend.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-3","iconValue":"donut","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"label":{"field":"status","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10","allOthers":true},"value":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"value":{}},"channels":{"label":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Cart Status"}},"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Donut","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"b3311b52-53da-47c3-a344-55c298c28b4e"}},"item-9":{"title":"3.2 Cart Abandonment Rate (%)","description":"DERIVED from 3.1 = abandoned carts \u00f7 (abandoned + purchased carts) \u00d7 100, restricted to carts that reached a final outcome (excludes still-active/emptied carts, same logic as a payment-failure-rate calc). Why it matters: turns 3.1's raw counts into a single benchmarkable rate. Action: track this weekly - a rising rate justifies investing in the discount-worklist (5.2) workflow; a flat/falling rate means the current recovery process is working.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-3","iconValue":"number","itemType":"chart","filters":[{"fieldPath":"status","disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":false,"values":["abandoned","purchased"]}}],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[{"fieldPath":"abandon_pct","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$cond\": [\n    {\n      \"$eq\": [\n        \"$status\",\n        \"abandoned\"\n      ]\n    },\n    100,\n    0\n  ]\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$cond\":[{\"$eq\":[\"$status\",\"abandoned\"]},100,0]}"}],"channels":{"value":{"field":"abandon_pct","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"mean"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{},"channels":{"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Custom"},"numberDecimals":{"enabled":true,"value":"1"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Number","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"731cb7a6-752e-4b21-bba7-7a185b853575"}},"item-10":{"title":"3.3 Abandoned Carts by Price Range (Foundation for 3.5)","description":"BASE. Raw single-field distribution of abandonment_alerts.unit_price, binned only for readability (25-unit bins) - not yet combined with any other field. Why it matters: shows on its own whether abandonment concentrates at low or high price points. Action: read alongside 3.4 before 3.5 combines both - don't conclude a price/quantity interaction from 3.5 without checking each dimension alone first.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-4","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"y":{"field":"unit_price","type":"nominal","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"category","isBinning":true,"quantitativeBinning":{"binSize":25}}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Abandoned Carts"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Unit Price"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"72632fb1-1ab8-4cc6-a5e5-b554226d62d2"}},"item-11":{"title":"3.4 Abandoned Carts by Quantity (Foundation for 3.5 & 3.6)","description":"BASE. Raw single-field distribution of abandonment_alerts.quantity - each bar is an exact stored quantity value, not a computed measure. Why it matters: shows on its own whether abandonment is mostly single-item or multi-item carts. Action: read alongside 3.3 before 3.5 combines both; note 3.6 later sums these same raw values per product.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-4","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"y":{"field":"quantity","type":"nominal","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"10"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Abandoned Carts"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Quantity"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"b8aa5f7c-2251-4a17-9948-d35c0b14ca1c"}},"item-12":{"title":"3.5 Abandoned Cart Concentration: Price \u00d7 Quantity (Combines 3.3+3.4)","description":"DERIVED - the same two raw fields shown separately in 3.3 and 3.4, now cross-tabulated: darker cells = more abandoned carts at that combination. Why it matters: a single-field view can hide an interaction only visible when both are considered together - e.g. single-item/high-price carts (hesitation) vs multi-item/low-price carts (shipping-cost sticker shock) can look identical in 3.3/3.4 alone. Action: match the recovery lever to the concentration zone - a payment-plan message for high-price clusters, a free-shipping nudge for multi-item clusters.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-4","iconValue":"heatmap","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"unit_price","type":"nominal","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"category","isBinning":true,"quantitativeBinning":{"binSize":25}},"y":{"field":"quantity","type":"nominal","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"category","isBinning":true,"quantitativeBinning":{"binSize":1}},"color":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{"categoryLabelAngle":{"enabled":true,"value":"diagonal"}}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Unit Price"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Quantity"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"color":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Abandoned Carts"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Heatmap","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"8560097e-1316-4517-a47a-c22272537d96"}},"item-13":{"title":"3.6 Top 5 Products by Units at Risk (Sums 3.4's Raw Values)","description":"DERIVED - takes the exact raw 'quantity' values shown per-cart in 3.4, now summed and grouped by product, ranked, limited to top 5. Why it matters: ranks recovery effort by size of opportunity - a product with 40 units abandoned outranks one with 3, even if both were abandoned equally often. Action: send the discount code (5.2) to sessions holding the top-ranked product first.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-4","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"x":{"field":"quantity","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"sum"},"y":{"field":"product_name","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"5"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Units at Risk"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Product"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"326ea819-3b40-4a29-8f83-57c8fc95f31c"}},"item-14":{"title":"4.1 Purchases per Minute (Bars) vs Revenue per Minute (Line)","description":"BASE \u2192 DERIVED. Bars = purchased carts per minute (count, from cart_status - single-writer, not duplicated). Line = revenue per minute (sum of unit_price \u00d7 quantity, computed here for the first time). Why it matters: their ratio in any minute is that minute's average order value - a widening gap means basket size is changing, not just purchase volume. Action: investigate any minute where the line rises without the bars rising - that's a shift in what's selling, not how much.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-3","iconValue":"combo-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[{"fieldPath":"status","disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":false,"values":["purchased"]}}],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[{"fieldPath":"minute_utc","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$dateToString\": {\n    \"format\": \"%m-%d %H:%M\",\n    \"date\": \"$cart_updated_at\",\n    \"timezone\": \"UTC\"\n  }\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$dateToString\":{\"format\":\"%m-%d %H:%M\",\"date\":\"$cart_updated_at\",\"timezone\":\"UTC\"}}"},{"fieldPath":"order_value","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$multiply\": [\n    \"$unit_price\",\n    \"$quantity\"\n  ]\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$multiply\":[\"$unit_price\",\"$quantity\"]}"}],"channels":{"x":{"field":"minute_utc","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","transformedType":"String","channelType":"category"},"y":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"ylines":{"field":"order_value","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"sum"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{"dataMarkers":{"enabled":true,"value":null}},"axes":{"x":{"categoryLabelAngle":{"enabled":true,"value":"diagonal"}},"ylines2":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Revenue"}}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Minute (UTC)"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Purchases"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"ylines":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Revenue"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Custom"},"numberDecimals":{"enabled":true,"value":"0"},"plotOnSecondaryAxis":{"enabled":true,"value":null}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Combo","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"e34e4871-51c8-4471-9d84-fa5418e92886"}},"item-15":{"title":"4.2 Average Order Value","description":"DERIVED = unit_price \u00d7 quantity (computed once in 4.1), averaged across every purchased cart. Why it matters: a single benchmarkable number for basket size, already visible as the implicit ratio in 4.1's two series. Action: track week over week - a falling AOV alongside a stable purchase count means shoppers are trading down, not buying less often.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-3","iconValue":"number","itemType":"chart","filters":[{"fieldPath":"status","disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":false,"values":["purchased"]}}],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[{"fieldPath":"order_value","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$multiply\": [\n    \"$unit_price\",\n    \"$quantity\"\n  ]\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$multiply\":[\"$unit_price\",\"$quantity\"]}"}],"channels":{"value":{"field":"order_value","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"mean"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{},"channels":{"value":{"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Custom"},"numberDecimals":{"enabled":true,"value":"2"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Number","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"218a29b8-8628-480f-ab68-44eb475c8b32"}},"item-16":{"title":"4.3 Revenue by Product, Top 5 (Sums 4.1/4.2's Order Value)","description":"DERIVED - the same per-cart order_value computed in 4.1/4.2, now summed and grouped by product, ranked, limited to top 5. Why it matters: identifies which products actually drive revenue, not just cart volume - a product can lead 3.6's abandonment list and still be a minor revenue contributor, or vice versa. Action: protect stock and pricing on whichever products lead here first; cross-check against 3.6 for the same product appearing on both lists.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-3","iconValue":"bar-grouped","itemType":"chart","filters":[{"fieldPath":"status","disabled":false,"type":"String","settings":{"allOthers":false,"values":["purchased"]}}],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[{"fieldPath":"order_value","rawExpression":"{\n  \"$multiply\": [\n    \"$unit_price\",\n    \"$quantity\"\n  ]\n}","derivedMQL":"{\"$multiply\":[\"$unit_price\",\"$quantity\"]}"}],"channels":{"x":{"field":"order_value","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"sum"},"y":{"field":"product_name","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category","isBinning":false,"isLimiting":true,"limitingSize":"5"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{},"axes":{"x":{}},"channels":{"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Revenue"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Custom"},"numberDecimals":{"enabled":true,"value":"0"}},"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Product"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Grouped Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"8997c19d-2de7-4eb7-a0b2-6b4d3d1a6db5"}},"item-17":{"title":"5.1 System Alerts by Type and Severity","description":"BASE synthesis. Every anomaly the consumers flagged in-stream: INCOMPLETE_FUNNEL_PURCHASE, SEARCH_GAP_DETECTED, HIGH_VALUE_ORDER, REPEAT_ABANDONER - the real-time output of the alert() calls in consumer.py, not a re-derived measure. Why it matters: this is the shortlist a manager reviews first thing, ranked by what's actually firing, not by what might be interesting. Action: HIGH severity items (REPEAT_ABANDONER, some HIGH_VALUE_ORDERs) get worked before MEDIUM/LOW.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-5","iconValue":"bar-stacked","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"y":{"field":"alert_type","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category"},"x":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"color":{"field":"severity","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{"colorDiscrete":{"enabled":true,"value":["#E6196E","#E6B219","#1392AB","#16CC62","#196EE6","#E65D19"]}},"axes":{},"channels":{"y":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Alert Type"}},"x":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"# Alerts"},"numberFormatting":{"enabled":true,"value":"Default"}},"color":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"Severity"}}},"conditionalFormatting":[]},"chartType":"Stacked Bar","meta":{},"sample":false,"query":null,"queryId":null,"interactiveFiltering":"highlight","embedding":{"id":"111f3d03-2980-4729-a05a-a399ba24b06f"}},"item-18":{"title":"5.2 Abandonment & Discount Worklist by Product (Most Derived)","description":"DERIVED - the most composite view on this dashboard: for each product, # alerts (3.1's 'abandoned' slice, grouped), total units at risk (same values summed in 3.6), average unit price (same field binned in 3.3), and suggested discount %. Why it matters: this is the actionable, exportable worklist behind every chart above it. Action: work down from the highest alert count; where average unit price is high, consider a smaller discount or a free add-on instead of a blanket 10% to protect margin.","dashboardId":"dashboard-1","dataSourceId":"data-source-4","iconValue":"data-table","itemType":"chart","filters":[],"missedFields":[],"lookupFields":[],"convertedFields":[],"calculatedFields":[],"channels":{"group":{"field":"product_name","type":"nominal","inferredType":"String","channelType":"category"},"value":{"field":"_id","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"String","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"count"},"value_series_0":{"field":"quantity","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"sum"},"value_series_1":{"field":"unit_price","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"mean"},"value_series_2":{"field":"discount_suggestion_pct","type":"quantitative","inferredType":"Number","channelType":"aggregation","aggregate":"mean"}},"reductions":{},"customisations":{"options":{"totalsColumn":{"enabled":false,"value":null}},"axes":{},"channels":{"group":{"labelOverride":{"enabled":true,"value":"